module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProperLimitStage.AffineBase
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitDescentGlueing.Glueing
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# A model of a proper morphism over a Noetherian stage of an affine base

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Limits/AffineNoetherianApproximation.lean` presents `Spec R`,
for an arbitrary commutative ring `R`, as the limit of the spectra of the subalgebras `ℤ[i]`
generated by the finite subsets `i` of `R`: every stage is affine, Noetherian and of finite type
over the integers, and every transition morphism is affine.
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProperLimitStage/AffineBase.lean` feeds that presentation to
[Stacks, Tag 081F] with Chow's lemma discharged, and so descends properness to a later stage.

Two spellings keep those pieces from composing, and this file removes both.

The first is a *spelling* of properness. Tag 081F is stated for a morphism `f₀ : X₀ ⟶ Y₀` of
objects of `CategoryTheory.Over (D.obj i₀)`, and asserts properness of
`((Over.pullback (D.map hi)).map f₀).left`. [Stacks, Tag 01ZM] part (1), which produces the model
in the first place, hands back an object `Xᵢ` of `Over (D.obj i)` and says nothing about any
morphism in that category; what a consumer has, and wants, is properness of the structure
morphism `((Over.pullback (D.map hi)).obj Xᵢ).hom`. The two differ by the isomorphism
`(Over.pullback π).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 _)) ≅ Over.mk (𝟙 _)`, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff` cancels.

The second is that Tag 01ZM part (1) produces its model only up to an isomorphism in
`Over (specAdjoinFinsetCone R).pt`, so properness has to be moved across that isomorphism before
Tag 081F will take it. `AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_hom_of_overIso` does that.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_hom_of_overIso`: properness of a structure morphism is invariant
  under isomorphism in a category of objects over a fixed base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff`: properness in Tag 081F's spelling is
  properness of the structure morphism of the base-changed object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isProper_overPullback_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`: Tag 081F at the
  Noetherian approximation of `Spec R`, in the base-change spelling.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isProper_model_of_isProper_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`: a separated
  finitely presented model of a proper morphism over `Spec R` becomes proper at a later stage.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isProper_model_of_finitePresentation_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`: the
  same with the model existentially quantified, which is the form Tag 01ZM part (1) delivers.

## Implementation notes

No Stacks attribute is attached. Tag 081F is stated for an arbitrary cofiltered system of
quasi-compact quasi-separated schemes with affine transitions and discharges Chow's lemma in the
quasi-compact quasi-separated case, [Stacks, Tag 0202]; the statements below are at one
particular system and still inherit `IsSeparated` on the model from the Noetherian case of Chow's
lemma, [Stacks, Tag 0200]. Both deviations are the ones
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProperLimitStage/NoetherianChow.lean` already records.

**Separatedness of the model is a hypothesis, not a conclusion, and that is the one gap left in
this step.** A proper morphism is separated, so the morphism over the limit is; but separatedness
at a *finite stage* is an eventual statement, [Stacks, Tag 086Q], which
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Limits/Descending/Separated.lean` proves as
`AlgebraicGeometry.eventually_isSeparated` for a system whose own limit is the scheme in
question. Applying it here means exhibiting the base changes of the model along the transitions
`j ⟶ i` as such a system, with limit the source of the morphism over `Spec R`. That construction
is not done here, so the model's separatedness is carried.

`AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff` is stated for an arbitrary morphism of
schemes and an arbitrary object over its target, because nothing in it is about this system; it
is the general fact that Tag 081F's conclusion, read at the structure morphism of an object
rather than at a morphism of objects, is properness after base change.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 081F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/081F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 086Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/086Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EX4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EX4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Properness of a structure morphism is invariant under isomorphism over the base.** If `X`
and `Y` are objects of `CategoryTheory.Over S` and `X ≅ Y` there, then `Y.hom` is proper as soon
as `X.hom` is. -/
theorem isProper_hom_of_overIso {S : Scheme.{u}} {X Y : Over S} (e : X ≅ Y) [IsProper X.hom] :
    IsProper Y.hom := by
  have hiso : IsIso e.hom.left := inferInstanceAs (IsIso ((Over.forget S).mapIso e).hom)
  have h : IsProper (e.hom.left ≫ Y.hom) := by
    rw [Over.w e.hom]
    infer_instance
  exact (MorphismProperty.cancel_left_of_respectsIso @IsProper e.hom.left Y.hom).mp h

/-- **Tag 081F's spelling of properness is properness after base change.** For `π : T ⟶ S` and
`X₀` an object over `S`, the morphism `X₀ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 S)` has proper left component after base
change along `π` exactly when the base change of `X₀` is proper over `T`.

The two differ by the structure morphism of `(Over.pullback π).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 S))`, which is an
isomorphism because it is a pullback of an identity. -/
theorem isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff {S T : Scheme.{u}} (π : T ⟶ S) (X₀ : Over S) :
    IsProper ((Over.pullback π).map
        (Over.homMk X₀.hom (Category.comp_id X₀.hom) : X₀ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 S))).left ↔
      IsProper ((Over.pullback π).obj X₀).hom := by
  have w := Over.w ((Over.pullback π).map
    (Over.homMk X₀.hom (Category.comp_id X₀.hom) : X₀ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 S)))
  have hiso : IsIso ((Over.pullback π).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 S))).hom := by
    dsimp [Over.pullback]
    infer_instance
  constructor
  · intro h
    rw [← w]
    infer_instance
  · intro h
    rw [← w] at h
    exact IsProper.of_comp _ ((Over.pullback π).obj (Over.mk (𝟙 S))).hom

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R]

/-- **Properness descends to a later stage of the Noetherian approximation of `Spec R`, in the
base-change spelling.** Let `i` be a finite subset of `R` and let `Xᵢ` be a scheme of finite
presentation and separated over `Spec ℤ[i]`. If the base change of `Xᵢ` to `Spec R` is proper,
then its base change to `Spec ℤ[j]` is proper for some finite `j ⊇ i`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isProper_baseChange_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram` — [Stacks, Tag
081F] at `AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetCone` — read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff` at `Xᵢ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 _)`. The two
compactness hypotheses that theorem places on the source are supplied by finite presentation:
quasi-compactness and quasi-separation of `Xᵢ.hom` over the quasi-compact quasi-separated
`Spec ℤ[i]`. -/
@[sga "3 VIB 10.1" "special case"]
theorem exists_isProper_overPullback_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram
    (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (Xᵢ : Over ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i))
    (hXᵢ : FinitePresentation Xᵢ.hom) [IsSeparated Xᵢ.hom]
    [IsProper ((Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetCone R).π.app i)).obj Xᵢ).hom] :
    ∃ (j : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (hj : j ⟶ i),
      IsProper ((Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).map hj)).obj Xᵢ).hom := by
  have hlfp : LocallyOfFinitePresentation Xᵢ.hom := hXᵢ.1
  have hqc : QuasiCompact Xᵢ.hom := hXᵢ.2.1
  have hqs : QuasiSeparated Xᵢ.hom := hXᵢ.2.2
  have hcs : CompactSpace Xᵢ.left := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace Xᵢ.hom
  have hqss : QuasiSeparatedSpace Xᵢ.left := quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated Xᵢ.hom
  have hmap : IsProper ((Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetCone R).π.app i)).map
      (Over.homMk Xᵢ.hom (Category.comp_id Xᵢ.hom) :
        Xᵢ ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i)))).left :=
    (isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff _ Xᵢ).mpr ‹_›
  obtain ⟨j, hj, hprop⟩ :=
    @exists_isProper_baseChange_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R _ i Xᵢ
      (Over.mk (𝟙 ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i)))
      (Over.homMk Xᵢ.hom (Category.comp_id Xᵢ.hom))
      hcs hqss (inferInstanceAs (QuasiSeparatedSpace ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i)))
      (inferInstanceAs (LocallyOfFiniteType Xᵢ.hom)) (inferInstanceAs (IsSeparated Xᵢ.hom))
      (inferInstanceAs (IsNoetherian ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i))) hmap
  exact ⟨j, hj, (isProper_overPullback_map_left_iff _ Xᵢ).mp hprop⟩

/-- **A separated finitely presented model of a proper morphism over `Spec R` becomes proper at a
later stage.** Let `X` be proper over `Spec R` and suppose `X` is, over `Spec R`, the base change
of a scheme `Xᵢ` of finite presentation and separated over `Spec ℤ[i]`. Then the base change of
`Xᵢ` to `Spec ℤ[j]` is proper for some finite `j ⊇ i`.

The isomorphism is the one [Stacks, Tag 01ZM] part (1) delivers; properness crosses it by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_hom_of_overIso`, after which this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isProper_overPullback_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`. -/
@[ega "IV 8.10.5" "(xii), special case", sga "4 VII 5.4" "partial"]
theorem exists_isProper_model_of_isProper_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram
    (X : Over (specAdjoinFinsetCone R).pt) [IsProper X.hom]
    (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (Xᵢ : Over ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i))
    (hXᵢ : FinitePresentation Xᵢ.hom) [IsSeparated Xᵢ.hom]
    (e : X ≅ (Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetCone R).π.app i)).obj Xᵢ) :
    ∃ (j : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (hj : j ⟶ i),
      IsProper ((Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).map hj)).obj Xᵢ).hom :=
  have := isProper_hom_of_overIso e
  exists_isProper_overPullback_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R i Xᵢ hXᵢ

/-- **Tag 081F composed with Tag 01ZM part (1) at the Noetherian approximation of `Spec R`.** Let
`X` be proper over `Spec R` and suppose that it admits, over `Spec R`, a model `Xᵢ` of finite
presentation and separated over some `Spec ℤ[i]`. Then that model is already proper over
`Spec ℤ[j]` for some finite `j ⊇ i`.

The hypothesis is the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 01ZM] part (1) at
`AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetCone`, strengthened by separatedness of the model — see the
implementation notes for why that strengthening is not discharged here. -/
theorem exists_isProper_model_of_finitePresentation_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram
    (X : Over (specAdjoinFinsetCone R).pt) [IsProper X.hom]
    (hmodel : ∃ (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (Xᵢ : Over ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i)),
      FinitePresentation Xᵢ.hom ∧ IsSeparated Xᵢ.hom ∧
        Nonempty (X ≅ (Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetCone R).π.app i)).obj Xᵢ)) :
    ∃ (i j : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (Xᵢ : Over ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i)) (hj : j ⟶ i),
      FinitePresentation Xᵢ.hom ∧
        IsProper ((Over.pullback ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).map hj)).obj Xᵢ).hom := by
  obtain ⟨i, Xᵢ, hXᵢ, _, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hmodel
  obtain ⟨j, hj, hprop⟩ :=
    exists_isProper_model_of_isProper_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R X i Xᵢ hXᵢ e
  exact ⟨i, j, Xᵢ, hj, hXᵢ, hprop⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
